diff --git a/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_runner_instruction.yaml b/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_runner_instruction.yaml
index 09b4f50..669e772 100644
--- a/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_runner_instruction.yaml
+++ b/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_runner_instruction.yaml
@@ -7,6 +7,15 @@ prompt: |
 
   First, consider whether this room type typically has wall decoration in real life.
   Utilitarian spaces may need no decoration at all - that's a valid outcome.
+  The authored room description is authoritative: when it explicitly says wall
+  context is optional, restrained, or must not be added merely to make the room
+  look fuller, and it names no required wall-mounted object, finish immediately
+  with no wall objects. Empty walls are the desired completed result in that case,
+  not an incomplete design. Do not ask the designer to invent decoration.
+
+  Optional background assets have a fail-open omission policy. If an optional
+  wall asset cannot be acquired or fails validation, omit it; do not rephrase it,
+  substitute another decoration, or start another generation batch to fill space.
 
   If decoration is appropriate:
   - Start with initial placement
diff --git a/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_agent.yaml b/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_agent.yaml
index a962b2f..f7300ab 100644
--- a/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_agent.yaml
+++ b/scenecode/prompts/data/wall_agent/stateful_planner_agent.yaml
@@ -27,6 +27,20 @@ prompt: |
   - Objects cannot overlap excluded regions (doors/windows)
   - Designer can control X (position along wall), Z (height), and rotation
 
+  # Authored Optional-Context Policy (takes priority over the generic workflow)
+  Inspect the room description before calling any agent. If it explicitly makes
+  wall context optional/restrained or forbids decoration added only to make the
+  room fuller, and it does not explicitly require a wall-mounted object, complete
+  this stage immediately with an empty wall-object set. Do not run the mandatory
+  placement workflow below merely because generic interior decoration often uses
+  clocks, shelves, boards, mirrors, or artwork.
+
+  If an optional background object is appropriate in another room, one failed
+  acquisition or validation means omit that object. Do not retry it under a
+  simplified description, replace it with a different decoration, or create a
+  new batch to achieve generic visual balance. Required authored wall objects are
+  not optional and keep their normal correction workflow.
+
   # Room Context
   {{ room_description }}
 
