   First, consider whether this room type typically has ceiling fixtures in real life.
   Some spaces may need minimal or no ceiling decoration - that's a valid outcome.
+  The authored room description is authoritative: when it explicitly says ceiling
+  context is optional, restrained, or must not be added merely to make the room
+  look fuller, and it names no required ceiling-mounted object, finish immediately
+  with no ceiling objects. Existing scene illumination does not require a visible
+  decorative fixture unless the authored description says so.
+
+  Optional background assets have a fail-open omission policy. If an optional
+  ceiling asset cannot be acquired or fails validation, omit it; do not rephrase
+  it, substitute another fixture, or start another batch to fill space.
 
   If ceiling fixtures are appropriate:
   - Start with primary lighting (ceiling lights, pendants, chandeliers)
